== {{dlc+|r}} Soul Stones ==
Soul Stones are all unlocked by beating both {{e|Hush}} and {{r|Boss Rush}} as their respective [[tainted character]]. They count as runes for the purposes of {{i|Clear Rune}} and {{i|Rune Bag}} and can spawn anywhere a rune can.
{{pickup table | Soul of Isaac, Soul of Magdalene, Soul of Cain, Soul of Judas, Soul of ???, Soul of Eve, Soul of Samson, Soul of Azazel, Soul of Lazarus, Soul of Eden, Soul of the Lost, Soul of Lilith, Soul of the Keeper, Soul of Apollyon, Soul of the Forgotten, Soul of Bethany, Soul of Jacob and Esau | main = yes | unlock method = yes}}{{dlc-}}

== Other ==
These are items other than cards and runes (and [[pill]]s) that take up the consumable slot. When on the ground, each of these items are uniquely identifiable by their respective icon. {{dlc+|r}} These consumables cannot be replicated by either {{i|Blank Card}} or {{i|Clear Rune}}, and {{i|Tarot Cloth}} has no effect on them, but the {{i|D1}} will always duplicate these into themselves.{{dlc-}}
{{pickup table | Cracked Key, Dice Shard, Emergency Contact | unlock method = yes }}{{dlc-}}

== Probabilities ==
Cards that spawn as random ones, i.e. with a sub-type of 0, have the following probabilities:
* Any tarot card (1-22) - 66.66%
** A specific tarot card - 3.03%
* Any reverse tarot card (56-77) - 11.22%
** A specific reverse tarot card - 0.51%
* Any face card (23-31) - 7.74%
** A specific face card (23-31) - 0.86%
* Queen of Hearts (79) - 0.86% (same as a specific face card)
* Any special card (42-54) - 3.51%
** A specific special card - 0.27%
* Cracked Key (78) - 0.27% (same as a specific special card)
* Wild Card (80) - 0.27% (same as a specific special card)
* Any rune (32-41) - 3.60%
** A specific rune - 0.36%
* Any soul stone (81-97) - 5.95%
** A specific soul stone - 0.35%
* Rune shard (55) - 0.00% (never spawns on a fully completed save file, chosen only as a replacement otherwise)

== Notes ==
* {{dlc|nr}} The game counts runes as cards for the purposes of {{i|Blank Card}}, and {{i|Tarot Cloth}}.
** {{dlc|r}} Even though runes no longer count as cards as of ''Repentance'', {{i|Little Baggy}} still prevents new runes from appearing except through forced drops (such as from {{i|Mom's Ring}} or {{i|Clear Rune}}). Runes that already existed prior to picking up Little Baggy will not be converted.
** {{i|Starter Deck}} does not prevent runes/soul stones from generating, will sometimes turn pills into either, and allows holding two of them.
* Runes will be replaced with cards if no runes are unlocked.
** {{dlc+|r}} However, items that normally spawn runes (e.g. {{i|Rune Bag}} or {{i|Clear Rune}}) can spawn Rune Shards before any runes are unlocked.{{dlc-}}
* If alternate versions of consumables have been unlocked (for example, {{E|Charged Key}}s or {{E|Mega Chest}}s), any cards that can spawn that type of consumables (for example, Ace of Spades or {{dlc|r}} VIII - Justice?) have a chance of being replaced with those rarer consumables.
** {{e|Key Ring|nr}}s are the only exception to this.
* {{dlc+|r}} If {{I|Tarot Cloth}} is held, the card will flash, indicating that it will be amplified by Tarot Cloth.{{dlc-}}
* {{Dlc+|r}} Using any teleport cards while inside of {{E|The Beast}} fight will simply move Isaac instantly to a different spot in the same room. This also includes the Joker card.{{dlc-}}

